    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "I found three errors and fixed them. I didn't re-render or re-query the drawing after the edits, so the fixes are unchecked.\n\n**1. What I changed** (no new entities)\n- **LN-011:** It sat on rd_EP but is the left shoulder edge (offset 20 L) on the T-2 tangent. I moved it to rd_ES.\n- **LN-016:** This is the right edge of pavement on T-2, but it was drawn at about 11 ft instead of 12 ft. I reset it to start at (2788.535, 1050.196) and end at (3965.240, 1442.431). Those are the 12 R points, taken from the endpoints of the neighbouring arcs AR-005 and AR-006.\n- **Callout \"EDGE OF PAVEMENT\":** The leader and arrowhead pointed at y=980, the rd_ES line at 20 R, not the edge of pavement. I moved the leader tip (LN-017 start) to (1702.633, 988.0), which is the rd_EP line LN-007 at 12 R. I moved the arrowhead PL-001 up 8 ft to match. The text and landing are unchanged.\n\n**2. Tool calls, in order**\n1. `get_document_state`\n2. `find_entities` with `detail: full`\n3. `modify_entity` on LN-011 with `layer: rd_ES`\n4. `modify_entity` on LN-016 with the new `start` and `end` above\n5. `modify_entity` on LN-017 with `start: [1702.6334039, 988.0]`\n6. `move_entities` on PL-001 with `delta: [0, 8]`\n\n**3. Problems and workarounds**\n- Nothing failed.\n- I computed the LN-016 coordinates myself. Offset 12 R is 8 ft closer to the centerline than the 20 R point. At the PT of the first curve, the 20 R point is (2791.065, 1042.606) and the centerline is (2784.740, 1061.580). So the 12 R point is the centerline plus 0.6 × (6.325, −18.974) = (2784.740 + 3.795, 1061.580 − 11.384) = (2788.535, 1050.196).\n- The far end comes from the AR-006 bounding box, (3965.240, 1442.431). Offsetting the centerline end (3961.445, 1453.815) the same way gives the same point.\n\nTwo things I did not change:\n- LN-016 and its neighbours LN-005 and LN-009 have no design anchor, whereas LN-004 and LN-007 do. I couldn't restore the anchor, since modify_entity edits fields and I wasn't sure it accepts an anchor.\n- I assumed the callout's text was right and the leader was wrong. If the intent was to call out the shoulder edge, the text would need changing instead."
